==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|ecto|plasm|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛktəˌplæzəm/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{lb|en|parapsychology}} The [[visible]] [[substance]] believed to [[emanate]] from the body of a [[spiritualistic]] [[medium]] during [[communication]] with the [[dead]].
# {{lb|en|parapsychology}} An [[immaterial]] or [[ethereal]] substance, especially the [[transparent]] [[corporeal]] presence of a spirit or [[ghost]].
# {{lb|en|cytology}} The outer [[granule]]-free layer of [[cytoplasm]].

